    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (77.12) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.72), our strongest starts of the day. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost that vaults him to the top of our rankings, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play, leveraging an elite .460 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against a vulnerable arm in J.T. Ginn. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.54) also projects as an elite play; his aggressive base-running upside is a premium asset in our 5x5 Roto structure, and he receives a substantial 14% platoon boost today, making him a critical weapon for securing our stolen base targets.\n\nManaging the volatility of today\u2019s lineups, we have opted to bench **Gary Sanchez** (38.24) despite his potential for power. **Gary Sanchez** fell just short of our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable matchup against Chris Sale and poor historical BvP numbers, which ultimately outweighed his raw output. We are also monitoring 37% rain risks for **Chase Meidroth** and **Carson Benge**; while both remain in the starting lineup for now, their scores are susceptible to mid-game interruptions. We continue to hold **Christian Yelich**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in reserve as we navigate the remaining game caps for the 2026 season.\n\nWe are carefully watching the L/L matchup for **Colt Keith** (50.79), whose score was dragged down by a 9% platoon penalty, and the matchup against a formidable arm in Cam Schlittler for **Kazuma Okamoto** (41.77), whose projection is severely hindered by the pitcher's elite 2.84 xERA. While **Trea Turner** (67.34) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.33) carry strong scores fueled by top-of-the-order positioning, we will be adjusting our late-inning sub-patterns if the precipitation in those venues increases, prioritizing the preservation of our limited remaining game appearances.",
